            <ArticleTitle>A 34-Year-Old Pregnant Woman With Cough, Chest Pain, and a Left Upper Lobe Mass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e87-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.chest.2016.03.008</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0012-3692(16)41672-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 34-year-old white woman who was 30 weeks' pregnant initially presented to her primary care physician with a cough for which she was given antibiotics, but she had persistent symptoms. These were followed by chest pain, as a result of which she was referred to our department. She had a past medical history of hypertension, and currently was in her sixth pregnancy, with no reported complications in the previous pregnancies. Review of systems was otherwise negative. She had a three-pack-year smoking history, but denied smoking during her current pregnancy.</AbstractText>
